|~ What is declared under `::each`, the step `*` runs on each
   element: its refusals. ~|

:each/PayloadNotQuoteError
  |~~ The payload of ::each is the quote of its body.
      ::link~(::each | doc)

      ~(
        42 | tag ::each
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::each/PayloadNotQuoteError ::number]
       )
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:each/ReadBackDiffersError
  |~~ The ::each prints as text that reads back as another step, or
      as none: a body holds at least one step.
      ::link~(::each | doc)

      ~(
        ~() | tag ::each
        !| [type /printed]
        |  eq [::each/ReadBackDiffersError "* ()"]
       )
  ~~|
  ::spec~()

:each/SubjectNotContainerError
  |~~ `*` runs its step on each element of a vector or a set, or on each
      value of a map; a value of another kind has no elements, and `|`
      runs a step on it whole.
      ::link~(::each | doc)

      ~(
        42 * add 1
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::each/SubjectNotContainerError ::number]
       )
  ~~|
  ::spec~()
